# Copy to .env for local development, or set these in your host's project
# settings (Vercel → Settings → Environment Variables) for production.
#
# VITE_-prefixed values are compiled into the browser bundle on purpose. Never
# put a secret behind that prefix — in particular, never the LTA account key.

# ─── Required ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# OneMap — plans every journey. Place search works without credentials, but
# public-transport routing needs a token. Register free at
# https://www.onemap.gov.sg/apidocs/register and set the email and password
# (the server exchanges them for a token and caches it)...
ONEMAP_EMAIL=
ONEMAP_PASSWORD=
# ...or, if you already hold a long-lived token, set this instead and leave the
# two above empty.
# ONEMAP_TOKEN=

# LTA DataMall — crowding, bus arrivals, service alerts, lift maintenance, road
# works. Free key: https://datamall.lta.gov.sg/content/datamall/en/request-for-api.html
LTA_ACCOUNT_KEY=

# The map base. OpenStreetMap is required as the geospatial base, and its tile
# policy forbids applications from using tile.openstreetmap.org, so OSM is
# served through MapTiler. Free, no card: https://cloud.maptiler.com/account/keys/
# Without this the map falls back to OneMap's own tiles, which are the Singapore
# Land Authority's national map rather than OpenStreetMap.
#
# VITE_ values are compiled into the browser bundle at BUILD time, not read at
# run time: setting this on a host only takes effect on the next deploy.
VITE_MAPTILER_KEY=

# ─── Optional ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Google AI Studio / Gemini. One server-side key powers three bounded helpers:
# report-photo consistency checks, commute-memory summaries, and ranking the
# real OneMap routes by preferences, weather and route events. Gemini never
# invents a route and its result always has a deterministic fallback.
#
# Create a key in Google AI Studio and keep it server-side. Do not use a VITE_
# prefix: that would expose the secret in the browser bundle. Gemini 2.5
# Flash-Lite has a free tier, subject to Google's current quotas and data terms.
#
# Leave this empty to keep the existing local rules and skip all AI calls.
# Demo mode never calls Gemini, even when a key is configured.
GEMINI_API_KEY=
# Optional model override. The default is the stable free-tier-capable model.
# GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-3.5-flash-lite

# Demo mode, for a stage and a venue network nobody controls. With this on, a
# live call that FAILS is answered from recorded data instead of an error — and
# every screen showing it says "Recorded", so nothing is passed off as live. It
# also offers a "week of sample trips" button so the learned-commute card can be
# shown without waiting a fortnight. One switch: the server reads this too.
# VITE_DEMO_MODE=1
